  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​] containing NNN integers.\n\nYou also have an integer KKK.\n\nYou can perform the following operation on this array:\n\n\nChoose indices iii and jjj such that ∣i−j∣≥K|i - j| \\geq K∣i−j∣≥K, and swap AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​.\n\nThat is, you can swap the values of two indices that are at a distance of at least KKK from each other.\nFind the lexicographically **smallest** array that can be reached, if you perform the above operation several (possibly, zero) times.\n\n**Note:** For two arrays XXX and YYY of the same length, XXX is said to be lexicographically smaller than YYY if there exists an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N) such that:\n\n\nX1=Y1,X2=Y2,…,Xi−1=Yi−1X_1 = Y_1, X_2 = Y_2, \\ldots, X_{i-1} = Y_{i-1}X1​=Y1​,X2​=Y2​,…,Xi−1​=Yi−1​; and\nXi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated numbers, the values A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, print on a new line NNN space-separated integers — the lexicographically smallest array possible after applying the above operation several times.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,K≤1051 \\leq N, K \\leq 10^51≤N,K≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
