        "input": "2\n3 2\n3 2 1\n4 3\n3 2 4 1",
        "output": "1 2 3\n1 2 4 3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Initially, we have A=[3,2,1]A = [3, 2, 1]A=[3,2,1].\nChoose i=1i = 1i=1 and j=3j = 3j=3, which is valid because ∣1−3∣=2≥K=2|1-3| = 2 \\geq K = 2∣1−3∣=2≥K=2.\nSwapping A1A_1A1​ and A3A_3A3​, we have the array [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3], which is the best we can do.\nTest case 222: A=[3,2,4,1]A = [3, 2, 4, 1]A=[3,2,4,1] and K=3K = 3K=3 here.\nThe only possible swap is i=1i = 1i=1 and j=4j = 4j=4; the other two elements can't be moved.\nPerforming this swap gives us A=[1,2,4,3]A = [1, 2, 4, 3]A=[1,2,4,3], which is the best we can do."
      }
